{
  "id": "find-all-duplicates-in-an-array",
  "questionId": "find-all-duplicates-in-an-array",
  "slug": "find-all-duplicates-in-an-array",
  "title": "Find All Duplicates in an Array",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Cyclic sort",
  "patterns": [
    "cyclic sort",
    "array"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "each value in [1, n] has a natural home index (value-1). if a value appears twice, only one copy can occupy that home - what happens to the other copy?",
    "run cyclic placement: for each index, while the value there doesn't match its home value and the home slot doesn't already hold the correct value, swap it home",
    "once placement is done, scan the array. any index i where nums[i] != i+1 holds a value that is a duplicate (its 'twin' already occupies its rightful home)",
    "collect those mismatched values into a result, and since you scan left to right by index they naturally come out sorted"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "returning values in the order they were found without sorting, when the array traversal order doesn't already guarantee ascending order",
    "infinite loop when swapping a duplicate value that already sits next to its twin, if the swap condition doesn't check whether the target slot already has the correct value",
    "using O(n) extra space with a hash map when O(1) extra space placement is expected"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given an array `nums` of length `n` where every value is in the\nrange `[1, n]`, and each value appears either once or exactly twice.\n\n**Return every value that appears twice, sorted in ascending order.**\n",
    "constraints": [
      "array length is n, every value is in range [1, n]",
      "each value appears once or exactly twice",
      "return the duplicated values sorted ascending"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "no duplicates at all (empty result)",
      "every value in the array is duplicated",
      "array of length 2 that's a single duplicate pair"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
